Yices SMT Solver
=============================================

Copyright (c) 2026, SRI International
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

This applies to the Yices source. This archive also contains GMP and
LibPoly. These are covered by the GNU Lesser General Public License; NOTICES
states which version applies to each and reproduces the required notices. A
relink kit for rebuilding against your own versions of those libraries is
published as a separate asset on the release page.


Content
-------

This distribution includes four solvers

  bin/yices       (for the Yices 2 language)
  bin/yices-smt   (for SMT-LIB 1.2)
  bin/yices-smt2  (for SMT-LIB 2.0)
  bin/yices-sat   (sat solver, DIMACS format)

and the Yices libraries and header files

  lib/__DYLIB__
  include/yices.h
  include/yices_types.h
  include/yices_limits.h
  include/yices_exit_codes.h


Examples and documentation are in the examples and doc directories.


The binaries and library were linked statically against GMP version __GMP__,
copyright Free Software Foundation (see NOTICES).


pkg-config
----------

The file lib/pkgconfig/yices.pc supports `pkg-config --cflags` and
`pkg-config --modversion` from the unpacked archive. The `--libs` and
`--static --libs` results do not produce a working link from the archive as
shipped. The archive has no unversioned shared-library link, so `-lyices`
selects libyices.a, and the private dependency archives named by Libs.private
are not included in lib/.

The installer creates the unversioned shared-library link but does not install
yices.pc.


Installation
------------

The library's install name is '@rpath/__DYLIB__'. A program that links against
it must supply a run-path, normally with
`-Wl,-rpath,/path/to/yices/lib` at link time, or set `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` at
run time.
This distribution includes a shell script to copy the files into an
installation prefix.
Just type

   sudo ./install-yices

from a terminal. This will copy the binaries in /usr/local/bin, the header
files in /usr/local/include, and the libraries in /usr/local/lib. It also
installs the legal record:

  /usr/local/share/doc/yices-2.8.0/LICENSE
  /usr/local/share/doc/yices-2.8.0/NOTICES
  /usr/local/share/doc/yices-2.8.0/PROVENANCE
  /usr/local/share/licenses/yices-2.8.0/     the license texts

Other installation choices are possible. Try ./install-yices --help
for more explanations.



For more information, please visit https://yices.csl.sri.com.

